[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
OpenSearch Dashboards 2.17.1 runs here on the Node.js 18 of the package node18
(the Node.js line of 2.17.1); node18 and node24 cannot be installed together, so
this package and kibana6 (on node24) do not go on one server.

There is no security plugin (securityDashboards) in this package: OpenSearch
Dashboards talks to OpenSearch over plain http without credentials
(opensearch.hosts, default http://localhost:9200). The rc script refuses to start
with a setting of a plugin the package does not have in %%ETCDIR%%/opensearch_dashboards.yml
(opensearch_security.* and the others it names: %%OSD_CONFIG_OUT%%):
OpenSearch Dashboards would stop at its start on them. Without the security plugin
everyone who reaches its port can do everything: keep it behind a firewall or a
proxy with authentication.

Not in this package: %%OSD_PLUGINS_OUT%% (why: the Makefile of the port).

The options of Node.js (--max-old-space-size and the like) go into
%%ETCDIR%%/node.options, one per line. Its log is rolled at 10 MB without
archives by newsyslog (%%PREFIX%%/etc/newsyslog.conf.d/opensearch_dashboards.conf);
service opensearch-dashboards reload opens it again.

Stop the service before this package replaces the official one: the rc script
keeps its pid file in /var/run/opensearch_dashboards/.
EOM
}
]
